! Diamond silicon in a 4-atom tetragonal cell: a1 = (a/2, a/2, 0),
! a2 = (-a/2, a/2, 0), a3 = (0, 0, a), which is half the conventional cubic
! cell and so holds four atoms. The same crystal as si2-paw-force.in, at twice
! the PAW sublattice -- it exists only to put a point between two atoms and
! eight on the one-centre atom dial's crossover.
 &control
    calculation = 'scf'
 /
 &system
    ibrav = 0, celldm(1) = 10.20, nat = 4, ntyp = 1,
    ecutwfc = 20.0, ecutrho = 160.0
 /
 &electrons
    conv_thr = 1.0d-8
 /
CELL_PARAMETERS alat
  0.50  0.50  0.00
 -0.50  0.50  0.00
  0.00  0.00  1.00
ATOMIC_SPECIES
 Si 28.086 Si.pbe-n-kjpaw_psl.0.1.UPF
ATOMIC_POSITIONS alat
 Si 0.00 0.00 0.00
 Si 0.25 0.25 0.25
 Si 0.00 0.50 0.50
 Si 0.25 0.75 0.75
K_POINTS automatic
 4 4 2 0 0 0
